course: dictionary
lesson: 11927
title: Calmness and the -ness ending
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Calmness is a noun, a word for a state or feeling. It comes from the adjective calm, which means quiet and peaceful, with the ending -ness added. «The calmness of the lake surprised the fishermen.» Here calmness names how the lake looked: still and peaceful.
explain: Calmness can describe a person too. «Her calmness helped everyone in the room stay safe.» She stayed quiet and unworried, even when things were scary. When you see -ness at the end of a word, check whether the root word is an adjective you already know.
explain: Calmness is uncountable, so we do not say "a calmness" or "two calmnesses". We use phrases like «with calmness», «keep calm» or «an air of calmness». «He answered the question with calmness.» Keep calm is a phrase with a verb, but calmness itself is the noun.
fact: Calmness means being quiet, peaceful and not worried, angry or excited.
fact: Calmness can also mean stillness in weather or water, as in «the calmness of the sea».
fact: The ending -ness changes an adjective into a noun: calm becomes calmness.
fact: In a fire drill or emergency, keeping calm helps you listen and follow instructions.
fact: Breathing slowly is one way to bring calmness to your body and mind.
exercise: «The sea was still, with the calmness of a lake.» What does calmness mean here? | Loud crashing waves | A sudden storm | *Stillness, like calm water with no waves | Cold weather only
exercise: Mia took a slow breath and spoke with calmness. What is calmness? | Anger and shouting | Tiredness after a long walk | Excitement about a game | *A quiet, peaceful state, not worried or upset
exercise: Calmness comes from an adjective. Find and copy that adjective. | *calm | calmness | answer | sea
test:
In a fire drill, what helps you follow the instructions? | Panic and running ahead | *Keeping calm and listening carefully | Shouting for your friends | Hiding under a desk without a word
Which word is the noun made from calm? | calmly | *calmness | calmer | calming
exam:
«The storyteller spoke with calmness, even as the storm grew.» What does calmness show about the storyteller? | Fear and panic | Anger at the crowd | *A quiet, unworried state of mind | Sleepiness
